.env
__pycache__
# Local tool settings and personal working notes — not part of the public repo.
.claude/settings.local.json
todos_and_thougts.txt
# ── Data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The pipeline is meant to be REPRODUCIBLE. The curated/public data INPUTS and the
# small Orbis-derived bridge tables are committed; the pipeline's own OUTPUTS are
# regenerable and are NOT committed. Specific exclusions:

# 1) Orbis raw — PROPRIETARY, must not be shared. Reproducibility is preserved
#    because the Orbis-DERIVED bridge tables it produces ARE committed (see §5),
#    so the Orbis-raw steps (3_1, 3_2, build_hq_shares_by_source,
#    build_cbcr_universe_*) can be skipped — everything from 1_8 onward reads them.
/data/raw/orbis/
/data/raw/resources/orbis_extractives_broad*.csv

# 2) Files over GitHub's 100 MB limit — large PUBLIC downloads. Obtain them per
#    the instructions in src/config.py, then re-run the pipeline.
/data/raw/gravity/
/data/raw/OECD.CTP.TPS,DSD_CBCR@DF_CBCRI,*.csv
# BaTIS bulk trade-in-services download (~2.8 GB; read by 1b_destination_based_sales.py):
/data/raw/OECD-WTO_BATIS_data_BPM6-1/
*.mp4

# 3) Provenance source documents (NOT read by any script — only the curated CSVs
#    extracted from them are). Excluded for now to keep the repo lean.
/data/raw/EITI reports/

# 4) Old-year archive — not needed to reproduce the current run.
/data/archive/

# 5) Pipeline OUTPUTS (intermediate working files + the final cbcr_main_* datasets)
#    are REGENERABLE by re-running, so they are not committed — EXCEPT the
#    Orbis-derived bridge tables (cannot be regenerated without the proprietary
#    Orbis raw) and the hand-curated effective_resource_cit_rates.csv.
/data/intermediate/**
/data/final/**
!/data/intermediate/**/
!/data/final/**/
!/data/intermediate/extractive/hq_shares_by_commodity_yearly.csv
!/data/intermediate/extractive/hq_shares_by_source_commodity_yearly.csv
!/data/intermediate/extractive/cbcr_universe_presence.csv
!/data/final/effective_resource_cit_rates.csv

# 6) Material NOT used by the current pipeline — provenance source documents
#    (company filings, government reports, images extracted from them) and
#    generated reports. Kept on disk for transparency / future use, but not
#    committed; the pipeline reads only the curated CSVs extracted from them.
# Resource/EITI source documents — keep ONLY the curated extraction tables:
/data/raw/resources/country sources/**
!/data/raw/resources/country sources/brazil_anp_extracted.csv
!/data/raw/resources/country sources/lesotho_revenue_extracted.csv
!/data/raw/resources/country sources/petrobras_union_dividends_extracted.csv
!/data/raw/resources/country sources/turkey_cit_extractive_extracted.csv
!/data/raw/resources/country sources/China_resource_tax_from_statistical_yearbooks.txt
!/data/raw/resources/country sources/resource_revenue_extracted_new.csv
# (The generated per-country resource reports in data/raw/country_resource_info/
#  ARE committed — kept as a reference deliverable.)
# Public CbCR report PDFs (provenance, not a pipeline input):
/data/raw/pCbCR/
# Climate-finance SOURCE workbooks (only the curated cpi_africa_*.csv are read):
/data/raw/climate_finance/*.xlsx
/data/raw/Data-Landscape-of-Climate-Finance-in-Africa-2024.xlsx
# Unused German trade-tax tables (only 71231-0001 is read, by the us_only sub-project):
/data/raw/corporate_taxes_germany/71231-0002_en/
/data/raw/corporate_taxes_germany/71231-0003_en/
/data/raw/corporate_taxes_germany/71231-0010_en/
/data/raw/corporate_taxes_germany/71231-0011_en/
/data/raw/corporate_taxes_germany/71231-0012_en/
# Other unused loose inputs / strays:
/data/raw/ReadMe_AAMNE.xlsx
/data/raw/CbcR_reporters_over_time.xlsx
/data/raw/cthi_unilateral_cross_scores.csv
/data/raw/Interactive Budget Dashboard 2026_Budget Data_Tabel.csv
/data/output/

# Keep the folder skeleton everywhere.
!**/.gitkeep


# ── Output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# output/ is REGENERABLE and enormous (~90 GB; unitary_taxation alone is 80 GB of
# per-spec result CSVs + bootstrap draws, several files over GitHub's 100 MB
# limit). Only the unitary-taxation DELIVERABLES are committed — the report
# FIGURES (.png), the headline .xlsx tables, and the small cross-sample summaries
# (across_samples/). Everything else (per-spec CSVs, the other analyses, archive)
# is ignored; regenerate by re-running scripts 5–9.
/output/**
!/output/**/
!/output/unitary_taxation/**/*.png
!/output/unitary_taxation/**/*.xlsx
!/output/unitary_taxation/across_samples/**
!**/.gitkeep


